From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:31:02 +0200
Subject: app: a fresh configuration starts fullscreen at the desktop's mode

Walnut is a console on a TV. Without a colobot.ini (a first start from the
menu) Colobot opened an 800x600 window. Now, when the configuration has
neither a Resolution nor a Fullscreen setting and no -resolution was
given, it starts fullscreen at the desktop's mode (1920x1080 on the PS3:
no mode change). A saved configuration, -resolution and the options menu
still decide.

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/src/app/app.cpp b/src/app/app.cpp
--- a/src/app/app.cpp
+++ b/src/app/app.cpp
@@ -600,6 +600,20 @@ bool CApplication::Create()
         std::vector<Math::IntPoint> modes;
         GetVideoResolutionList(modes);
 
+        // Walnut (a console on a TV): a fresh configuration starts fullscreen at the desktop's mode
+        // instead of an 800x600 window; a saved Resolution and Fullscreen, -resolution and the
+        // options menu still decide
+        if ( !m_resolutionOverride && !GetConfigFile().GetStringProperty("Setup", "Resolution", sValue) &&
+             !GetConfigFile().GetIntProperty("Setup", "Fullscreen", iValue) )
+        {
+            SDL_DisplayMode desktop;
+            if (SDL_GetDesktopDisplayMode(0, &desktop) == 0 && desktop.w > 0 && desktop.h > 0)
+            {
+                m_deviceConfig.size = Math::IntPoint(desktop.w, desktop.h);
+                m_deviceConfig.fullScreen = true;
+            }
+        }
+
         if ( GetConfigFile().GetStringProperty("Setup", "Resolution", sValue) && !m_resolutionOverride )
         {
             std::istringstream resolution(sValue);
